eficit of \u00a3852k driven by voids from regulatory compliance works","lead":"Shows operational pressure on housing service from regulatory compliance costs. While managed through reserves this year, signals ongoing structural pressure affecting HRA sustainability.","iso":"2026-09-29","paper_title":"Mid Devon DC Auditor&#39;s Annual Report 2025-26 Draft for Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://democracy.middevon.gov.uk/documents/s36672/36672.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Unresolved social rent calculation liability remains outstanding with DWP","lead":"Represents both a control failure (wrong rents charged for years undetected) and an unquantified contingent liability dependent on DWP settlement.","iso":"2026-09-29","paper_title":"Mid Devon DC Auditor&#39;s Annual Report 2025-26 Draft for Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://democracy.middevon.gov.uk/documents/s36672/36672.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Mid Devon DC Auditor&#39;s Annual Report 2025-26 Draft for Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://democracy.middevon.gov.uk/documents/s36672/36672.pdf","headline":"Three categories of governance recommendations remain unimplemented after 2\u20133 years of audit recommendations","detail":"Repeated recommendations: (1) Risk mapping to corporate objectives recommended since 2023/24; partial progress (9 of 15 risks mapped as of Feb 2026). (2) Central gifts and hospitality register recommended since 2023/24; council promised Jan 2026 publication but not delivered; using physical log. (3) Compliance assurance mechanism (periodic member/officer declarations) recommended since 2022/23; no progress.","category":"governance","matters":"Persistent failure to implement governance recommendations across multiple audit cycles suggests weak implementation discipline or low prioritisation of soft controls.","figures":"Not specified","quote":"The Council does not include its corporate objectives or key performance indicators alongside the reporting of risks.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Mid Devon DC Auditor&#39;s Annual Report 2025-26 Draft for Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://democracy.middevon.gov.uk/documents/s36672/36672.pdf","headline":"Housing Revenue Account deficit of \u00a3852k driven by voids from regulatory compliance works","detail":"HRA reported \u00a3852k deficit in 2025/26. Key drivers: high void levels required by updated Decent Homes Standard and Awaab's Law implementation caused lost rental income while properties underwent remedial works and incurred higher reinstatement costs. Deficit was offset by transfer from HRA Housing Maintenance Earmarked Reserve.","category":"overspend","matters":"Shows operational pressure on housing service from regulatory compliance costs. While managed through reserves this year, signals ongoing structural pressure affecting HRA sustainability.","figures":"\u00a3852k deficit","quote":"The Housing Revenue Account reported a deficit outturn \u00a3852k. Key drivers of the overspend were high levels of voids due to works to needed to comply with changes to the Decent Homes Standard and the introduction of Awaab's Law.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Mid Devon DC Auditor&#39;s Annual Report 2025-26 Draft for Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://democracy.middevon.gov.uk/documents/s36672/36672.pdf","headline":"Unresolved social rent calculation liability remains outstanding with DWP","detail":"Historic issue: council failed to set tenant rents to formula requirements for many years. Made refund payments of \u00a3780k in 2025/26 to non-welfare tenants. Provision reduced from \u00a31.8m (2024/25) to \u00a3921k (2025/26). Council remains in discussions with DWP over settlement for welfare-recipient tenants, leaving final liability uncertain.","category":"governance","matters":"Represents both a control failure (wrong rents charged for years undetected) and an unquantified contingent liability dependent on DWP settlement.","figures":"\u00a3921k provision remaining; \u00a3780k refunds paid in 2025/26; prior provisions \u00a31.8m (2024/25), \u00a31.5m (2023/24)","quote":"The Council remains in discussions with the DWP over the rectification of this issue for tenants in receipt of housing benefit and Universal Credit.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Mid Devon DC Auditor&#39;s Annual Report 2025-26 Draft for Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://democracy.middevon.gov.uk/documents/s36672/36672.pdf","headline":"General Fund projected three-year deficit fell from \u00a313.3m to \u00a34.5m between September 2025 and February 2026 with no explanation","detail":"September 2025 MTFP identified cumulative deficits of \u00a33.35m (2026/27), \u00a34.7m (2027/28) and \u00a35.79m (2028/29) totalling \u00a313.3m. February 2026 update achieved a balanced 2026/27 and reset projections to \u00a31.2m (2027/28), \u00a31.3m (2028/29) and \u00a32m (2029/30) totalling \u00a34.5m. The \u00a38.8m reduction is not explained in the report.","category":"savings","matters":"A two-thirds reduction in projected deficits signals either substantial unplanned savings or unrealistic budget assumptions. A lender must understand which.","figures":"Sept 2025: \u00a33.35m, \u00a34.7m, \u00a35.79m (\u00a313.3m cumulative); Feb 2026: \u00a31.2m, \u00a31.3m, \u00a32m (\u00a34.5m cumulative)","quote":"The General Fund MTFP identified deficits of \u00a33.35m for 2026/27, \u00a34.7m for 2027/28 and \u00a35.79m in 2028/29. The cumulative budget gap over the three years is \u00a313.3m.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-29","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Mid Devon DC Auditor&#39;s Annual Report 2025-26 Draft for Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://democracy.middevon.gov.uk/documents/s36672/36672.pdf","headline":"Housing Revenue Account contained material accounting error reversing income and expenditure classification","detail":"The HRA Income and Expenditure Account was materially misstated, showing net income when it should have shown net expenditure. This was identified during audit procedures and corrected.","category":"audit","matters":"Material errors in housing accounts represent control gaps in a major council service and indicate weak preventative controls.","figures":"Material error amount not disclosed","quote":"The Housing Revenue Account (HRA) Income and Expenditure Account contained a material error that led to the Account showing a net income on HRA Services for the year when it should have been net expenditure.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-01"},"name":"Mid Devon","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-23","since_iso":"2026-08-24","distress":false,"headline":"2027/28 balance assumes \u00a3600k benefit from revised business rates forecast that requires validation","lead":"Unvalidated income assumptions create risk that the stated balanced budget position may not materialise if business rates forecasts prove optimistic","also":["4 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Scrutiny Committee on 2026-09-28","n_findings":5,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Cabinet Report - MTFP August 2026","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.middevon.gov.uk/documents/s36411/36411.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":89,"news_drafts_total":3}}